{
  "title": "Chapter 25: Climate Classification",
  "order": 222,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Climate classification is the scientific method of grouping different regions of the world based on their long-term weather patterns such as temperature, precipitation, humidity, and seasonal variations. Since climate directly influences vegetation, agriculture, settlement, and economic activities, geographers developed classification systems to simplify the complex climatic diversity of the Earth.",
      "id": "jga8tau"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
