    {
      "id": "y373knw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Weather vs Climate"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Climate classification simplifies global weather diversity by grouping regions based on temperature, precipitation, humidity, and seasonality.",
        "The Köppen Climate Classification is the most widely used system because it objectively links temperature and rainfall data with natural vegetation zones.",
        "Köppen's major climate categories include Tropical (A), Dry (B), Warm Temperate (C), Continental (D), and Polar (E).",
        "Thornthwaite's system relies on moisture availability and the precipitation effectiveness (PE) index to evaluate water balance.",
        "India predominantly experiences a Tropical Monsoon climate designated as 'Am' under Köppen's classification."
      ],
      "id": "40q4i0k"
    },
