      "content": "12. Advantages of Köppen Classification"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Köppen classification is vegetation-based and uses combinations of capital and lowercase letters.",
        "Mediterranean climate is represented by the symbol 'Cs', while Tundra is represented by 'ET'.",
        "India is primarily classified under the 'Am' (Tropical Monsoon) climate type.",
        "Thornthwaite's classification is based on water balance using the Precipitation Effectiveness (PE) index."
      ],
      "id": "22jn29q"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Simple and objective.",
      "id": "2yrmopz"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Closely matches vegetation zones.",
      "id": "modkpdu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Uses measurable data.",
      "id": "whpanhw"
    },
    {
      "id": "utf0sfh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13. Limitations"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Does not fully consider wind patterns.",
      "id": "bxpw0iu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Ignores extreme weather events.",
      "id": "wzxtq2m"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Boundaries are sometimes artificial.",
      "id": "g72vv5e"
    },
